# Telegram Bot API (server-only — never commit real values)
# 1. Create a bot with @BotFather and copy the token
# 2. Add the bot to your group and grant it permission to send messages
# 3. Set TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID to the group id (usually starts with -100)
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Optional Nuxt-prefixed aliases (same values; useful in some hosts)
# NUXT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# NUXT_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Content intake bot — collect landing-page copy from the school
# Run locally (long-polling; does not affect GitHub Pages):
#   npm run intake:telegram
# Then open the bot in Telegram and send /start
#
# After each production update:
# 1. Commit content/code and push to main (GitHub Actions rebuilds the static site)
# 2. Wait until the "Deploy GitHub Pages" workflow is green
# 3. In ArvanCloud CDN: purge cache for HTML (/ and pages) — and for /images + /_ipx if photos changed
# 4. Hard-refresh the live site (Ctrl+Shift+R). GitHub Pages itself caches ~10 minutes.
